# Forms staging area: source PDFs, extracted .fields.json, converted out/ and
# qa/ page renders. ~33MB of regenerable binaries whose converted output only
# differs from the committed templates in form-template-export/ by stray blank
# fields. Keep it local; the promoted templates are what the repo ships.
auth-server/form-template-export/_incoming/
# Same staging pattern for the BC batch: government source PDFs, manifests and
# QA renders. Only the promoted BC*_.pdf/.json templates belong in the repo.
auth-server/form-template-export/_incoming_bc/
auth-server/form-template-export/_incoming_bc2/
# Batch 3 stages the two King's Printer consolidations as well, since the
# child-protection and adoption forms are cut out of them.
auth-server/form-template-export/_incoming_bc3/
# And for the Ontario batch: government sources, the headless XFA flatten and
# QA renders. The promoted FormXX.pdf/.json templates are what the repo ships.
auth-server/form-template-export/_incoming_on/
# And for the Saskatchewan batch: King's Printer source PDFs, the manifest and
# QA renders. Only the promoted SKKB_*.pdf/.json templates belong in the repo.
auth-server/form-template-export/_incoming_sk/
# And for the Manitoba batch: Manitoba Justice source PDFs, the manifest and QA
# renders. Only the promoted MBKB_*.pdf/.json templates belong in the repo.
auth-server/form-template-export/_incoming_mb/
# pdf.js vendor build used by the headless XFA flatten, plus the source PDFs
# staged for it. Fetched by tools/bc-forms/xfa/fetch_pdfjs.sh, not committed.
auth-server/tools/bc-forms/xfa/pdf.mjs
auth-server/tools/bc-forms/xfa/pdf.worker.mjs
auth-server/tools/bc-forms/xfa/pdf_viewer.css
auth-server/tools/bc-forms/xfa/cmaps/
auth-server/tools/bc-forms/xfa/standard_fonts/
auth-server/tools/bc-forms/xfa/srcs/
auth-server/tools/bc-forms/xfa/srcs2/
